  "synopsis": "Thwarted again by Naraku, Inuyasha, Kagome Higurashi, and their friends must continue their hunt for the few remaining Shikon Jewel shards, lest they fully form into a corrupted jewel at the hands of Naraku. But Naraku has plans of his own to acquire them, and will destroy anyone and anything standing in his way—even his own underlings.\n\nThe persistent, unyielding danger posed by Naraku forces Sango and Miroku to decide what is most important to them—each other or their duty in battle. Meanwhile, Inuyasha must decide whether his heart lies with Kikyou or Kagome, before fate decides for him. Amid the race to find the shards, Inuyasha and his brother Sesshoumaru must also resolve their feud and cooperate for their final confrontation with Naraku, as it is a battle they must win in order to put a stop to his evil and cruelty once and for all.\n\n[Written by MAL Rewrite]",
  "synopsis_es": "Frustrados nuevamente por Naraku, Inuyasha, Kagome Higurashi y sus amigos deben continuar su búsqueda de los pocos fragmentos restantes de la Joya Shikon, para que no se conviertan completamente en una joya corrupta a manos de Naraku. Pero Naraku tiene sus propios planes para adquirirlos y destruirá a cualquiera que se interponga en su camino, incluso a sus propios subordinados.\n\nEl peligro persistente e inquebrantable que representa Naraku obliga a Sango y Miroku a decidir qué es más importante para ellos: el uno al otro o su deber en la batalla. Mientras tanto, Inuyasha debe decidir si su corazón está con Kikyou o con Kagome, antes de que el destino decida por él. En medio de la carrera para encontrar los fragmentos, Inuyasha y su hermano Sesshoumaru también deben resolver su enemistad y cooperar para su enfrentamiento final con Naraku, ya que es una batalla que deben ganar para poner fin a su maldad y crueldad de una vez por todas.\n\n[Escrito por MAL Rewrite]",
